desktop-shell: remove apps from the Start menu (right click)

Right-clicking an app in the Start menu (in the main list or in a folder)
opens its context menu at the pointer: open it, pin or unpin it on the
taskbar, and "Remove from Start menu". Removed apps are saved in
~/.config/hexaos/start-hidden (one launcher name per line, like
taskbar-pins) and stay out of the menu after restarting the desktop; a
pinned app stays on the taskbar. A folder whose apps are all removed is
not shown.

When some app was removed, the Start button's right-click menu gets
"Restore removed Start apps", which brings every one of them back.

The shell shows one popup at a time, so the Start menu closes first and
the context menu opens from popups_close_task.

